 # packages/cli bundles bake build-time absolute paths; Turbo cache shared across worktrees replayed pi13 paths
 
-Symptom (2026-10-17): every new `sandpiper` launch fails at startup with ENOENT for /Users/dstephen/git/sandpiper-ai-pi13/node_modules/jsdom/lib/jsdom/browser/default-stylesheet.css, after the pi13 jj workspace was removed. Reproduced with `bun run --bun node_modules/.bin/sandpiper --help`.
+## 2026-10-18T00:28:10.820Z
 
-Root cause (two parts):
-1. Bundles are not relocatable. Bun's bundler inlines `__dirname`/`__filename` as build-time absolute paths. The packages/cli bundles (dist/chunks/sandpiper_resources-*.js, dist/chunks/system_prompt_diagnostic-*.js, dist/standalone/chunks/sandpiper_standalone-*.js) embed three absolute paths into node_modules: better-sqlite3/lib, jsdom/lib/jsdom/living/css/helpers (reads default-stylesheet.css at load), and jsdom/lib/jsdom/living/xhr/xhr-sync-worker.js.
-2. Turborepo shares the local cache across Git worktrees when turbo.json sets no cacheDir (documented: https://turborepo.dev/docs/reference/configuration). jj 0.46 `workspace add` creates a Git worktree in colocated repos, so the AGENT-307 builds in ../sandpiper-ai-pi13 wrote to the default workspace's .turbo/cache. Entry b3e9c76a36a1dee2 (packages/cli build, created 2026-10-16 12:24 during the pi13 work, base sha ed93a550 plus the dirty bump) contains pi13 paths. After landing, the default workspace's sources hashed identically, so its 13:10 rebuild was a cache hit that restored the pi13-built dist.
+- **description**: added (10 lines)
+- **related**: (none) → TOOLS-30, AGENT-307
 
-Fix options:
-- Unblock: rebuild packages/cli without the cache (TURBO_FORCE=1) in the default workspace.
-- Guard: set "cacheDir": ".turbo/cache" in turbo.json to stop cross-worktree sharing (loses cache hits between workspaces).
-- Root fix: make bundles relocatable (externalize jsdom and better-sqlite3 from the bundles, or inline the asset/paths with a build plugin like devtools' cssTreeBundledDataPlugin). With relocatable outputs, cross-worktree cache sharing becomes safe again. Interacts with TOOLS-30 (build simplification) and the compiled app.
